+# Act34 measured follow-on envelope plan — 2026-11-24T18:40Z
+
+**Office:** Ministry of Economy (Act 29). **Scope:** resource-evidence method for waves *after* the first genuine four-office wave. Not law, permit, activation, dispatch, allocation, staffing plan, or spending authority. No office is activated by this record.
+
+## Trigger and evidence
+Apply only after the first four-office wave has actually dispatched and all four offices reach terminal (or explicitly held) state. Until then the proxy p95 in `records/economy/2026-11-24-act34-measured-envelope.md` remains the only defensible planning bound: per office 11,320,103 tokens / 7,987 CPU-s `UPPER_BOUND` / 1,997 wall-s; aggregate 45,280,412 tokens / 31,948 CPU-s / 7,988 summed office-wall-s.
+
+Read, do not invent:
+- `government/knowledge-budget-tool.py snapshot|delta|aggregate`: authoritative `session_v2` five token fields (`tokens_input`, `tokens_output`, `tokens_reasoning`, `tokens_cache_read`, `tokens_cache_write`), monotonic wall seconds, and the 45-day cumulative ledger with `by_office`.
+- host `/proc/stat` busy delta: whole-host CPU `UPPER_BOUND`, deliberately charged to each overlapping office; not per-office CPU attribution.
+- wave start/end `state/economy/resources.json`, funding `report.json`, and the board/project artifact (or absence) for each office. Peak four-office memory remains `UNAVAILABLE` unless sampled during the wave.
+
+## Computation per completed wave
+1. For each office record an observed vector: `tokens_total` (sum of five fields), `wall_seconds`, `cpu_seconds_upper_bound`, `peak_memory` (or null), and whether a delivered outcome exists. Preserve failures, stops and ambiguous exits as observations.
+2. Planning envelope for the next wave before three comparable waves: `max(proxy p95, observed max)` per metric. After three comparable waves: observed p95, but never below the proxy p95 without an explicit reason and never above it without the row that caused the change.
+3. Remaining headroom from the non-resettable ledger: `remaining_aggregate[k] = aggregate_cap[k] - ledger_aggregate[k]` and `remaining_office[k] = per_office_cap[k] - ledger_by_office[k]` for each of tokens/CPU/wall. A follow-on wave is admissible only if its planned envelope is within *both* remainders for all three metrics. `government/knowledge-practical-bounds.py ambiguous` holds the full charge on kill/overrun/ambiguous exit; reconcile before planning another wave.
+4. Resource-specific admissibility: no `critical` disk/memory/CPU status, at least two independent free provider routes with no active hard cooldown, and no new paid/Luna fallback. If a resource is `short` or funding is `elevated`, report that constraint; do not turn it into a staffing instruction.
+5. Publish the observed rows and revised envelope in `records/economy/` with the wave commit/session IDs. Any cap or permit change remains an Executive decision under Act34; Economy only supplies measured evidence.
+
+## Current position (not a first-wave result)
+All four activation rows disabled and cumulative ledger zero at last read. Live caps are 400,000 tokens / 1,800 CPU-s / 3,600 wall-s per office and 1,600,000 / 7,200 / 14,400 aggregate — below one proxy-p95 wave. Resource report 18:06Z: disk state `short` (82.2% used, 39.3 GiB free, ~2,143 h to full), memory spare 6.2 GiB, CPU busy 3.12/4 with load `watch`, free availability 4/13 and failover `elevated`. The existing Town Hall disk `NEEDS-FOUNDER:` line is unchanged and not repeated.
+
+No new spending, no training-data route, no Soring work, no dispatch claim.
